WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.327
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.627 --> 00:00:08.990
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:14.752
Unit twenty: Transport of the Future. In this unit, you will make predictions about the future.

4
00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:16.647
Electric.

5
00:00:17.347 --> 00:00:19.903
Electric means using electricity to work.

6
00:00:20.203 --> 00:00:22.017
Electric cars are quiet.

7
00:00:22.717 --> 00:00:25.161
Your turn. Say: Electric.

8
00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:28.769
Electric.

9
00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:30.982
Driverless.

10
00:00:31.682 --> 00:00:34.146
Driverless means able to drive without a person.

11
00:00:34.446 --> 00:00:37.502
Driverless taxis already exist in some cities.

12
00:00:38.202 --> 00:00:41.423
Your turn. Say: Driverless.

13
00:00:44.123 --> 00:00:45.229
Driverless.

14
00:00:46.217 --> 00:00:47.113
Train.

15
00:00:47.813 --> 00:00:50.788
Train means a line of carriages that travels on rails.

16
00:00:51.088 --> 00:00:53.738
A fast train could link Phnom Penh and Bangkok.

17
00:00:54.438 --> 00:00:56.881
Your turn. Say: Train.

18
00:00:59.581 --> 00:01:00.211
Train.

19
00:01:01.217 --> 00:01:01.951
Bike.

20
00:01:02.651 --> 00:01:04.047
Bike means a bicycle.

21
00:01:04.347 --> 00:01:06.276
More people will ride bikes.

22
00:01:06.976 --> 00:01:09.199
Your turn. Say: Bike.

23
00:01:11.899 --> 00:01:12.633
Bike.

24
00:01:13.617 --> 00:01:14.478
Pollution.

25
00:01:15.178 --> 00:01:17.526
Pollution means dirty air, water or land.

26
00:01:17.826 --> 00:01:20.000
Electric buses cause less pollution.

27
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.085
Your turn. Say: Pollution.

28
00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:26.589
Pollution.

29
00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:28.364
Future.

30
00:01:29.064 --> 00:01:30.982
Future means the time after now.

31
00:01:31.282 --> 00:01:33.270
What will cities look like in the future?

32
00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:36.193
Your turn. Say: Future.

33
00:01:38.893 --> 00:01:39.685
Future.

34
00:01:40.683 --> 00:01:41.580
Will.

35
00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:45.011
Will means used to say what we think is certain to happen.

36
00:01:45.311 --> 00:01:46.614
Cars will be electric.

37
00:01:47.314 --> 00:01:49.862
Your turn. Say: Will.

38
00:01:52.562 --> 00:01:53.238
Will.

39
00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:55.065
Fast.

40
00:01:55.765 --> 00:01:57.382
Fast means moving quickly.

41
00:01:57.682 --> 00:01:59.774
Future trains will be very fast.

42
00:02:00.474 --> 00:02:02.697
Your turn. Say: Fast.

43
00:02:05.397 --> 00:02:06.154
Fast.

44
00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:09.231
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:09.531 --> 00:02:12.273
Sreypich, how will people travel in the future?

46
00:02:13.583 --> 00:02:15.269
I think cars will be electric.

47
00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:17.921
Will they need drivers?

48
00:02:19.217 --> 00:02:20.914
Some might be driverless!

49
00:02:22.217 --> 00:02:23.914
What about flying taxis?

50
00:02:25.217 --> 00:02:28.354
People might fly in taxis, but I'm not sure.

51
00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:31.940
Grammar focus: Will and might.

52
00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:35.345
Cars will be electric. People might fly in taxis.

53
00:02:35.645 --> 00:02:38.805
Use 'will' when you are sure and 'might' when you are not sure.

54
00:02:39.817 --> 00:02:42.957
Now read and listen. Travelling in 2050.

55
00:02:43.257 --> 00:02:45.663
In the future, transport will change a lot.

56
00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:49.983
Cars will be electric, and some might be driverless.

57
00:02:51.283 --> 00:02:53.805
Fast trains will connect cities across Asia.

58
00:02:55.117 --> 00:02:57.662
More people will ride bikes in green cities.

59
00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.669
There will be less pollution, and the air will be cleaner.

60
00:03:02.983 --> 00:03:05.438
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:05.738 --> 00:03:08.077
Cars blank be electric. (sure)

62
00:03:08.377 --> 00:03:11.079
A, will. B, might. C, are.

63
00:03:15.083 --> 00:03:17.385
The answer is A: will.

64
00:03:18.883 --> 00:03:21.721
People blank fly in taxis. (not sure)

65
00:03:22.021 --> 00:03:24.758
A, might. B, will. C, are.

66
00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:30.889
The answer is A: might.

67
00:03:32.383 --> 00:03:34.696
Able to drive without a person means blank.

68
00:03:34.996 --> 00:03:39.149
A, driverless. B, electric. C, fast.

69
00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:45.614
The answer is A: driverless.

70
00:03:47.117 --> 00:03:50.756
Now it's your turn to speak. How will people travel in the future?

71
00:03:56.056 --> 00:04:01.506
I think people will use electric buses and trains. Some people might travel in flying cars!

72
00:04:01.806 --> 00:04:03.933
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:08.879
Great work today! You learned eight new words and will and might.

74
00:04:09.179 --> 00:04:13.446
Today's value is imagination. Imagine new ideas for a better future.

75
00:04:13.746 --> 00:04:16.340
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

76
00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:19.153
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

